# econ dashboard — optional environment overrides
# Add settings to /opt/econ/.env on the server; preserve any existing settings.
# systemd loads this file; install.sh restricts it to mode 0600.
# Use one KEY=value per line. Put comments on separate lines, not after values.
# The setup CLI reads this simple format without executing shell expressions.
# The systemd unit sets ECON_PORT; override it here if needed.

ECON_PORT=8080
# Background refresh cadence, seconds.
# ECON_REFRESH=300
# Sample data, no market network requests; automatic Telegram alerts suppressed.
# ECON_DEMO=1

# Reserved for the future: a free FRED API key would unlock extra panels
# (register at https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html).
# FRED_API_KEY=

# Stocks tab delayed quotes (~15-min delayed keyless overlay for displayed picks;
# filters and rank order stay anchored to settled daily closes).
# Disable the delayed-quote overlay entirely:
# ECON_STOCK_QUOTES=0
# Delayed-quote cache TTL in seconds (min 60, default 300):
# ECON_STOCK_QUOTE_TTL=300

# Telegram stock-movement alerts — opt-in; see README "Telegram stock alerts".
# Keep the real token in /opt/econ/.env only. Never commit it or paste it in chat.
# ECON_TELEGRAM_ENABLED=1
# ECON_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# ECON_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
# Shared by the dashboard sharp-rise badge and Telegram (default 3 percent).
# ECON_STOCK_ALERT_THRESHOLD=3
# Reject notification quotes older than 30 minutes (60-3600 seconds).
# ECON_TELEGRAM_MAX_QUOTE_AGE=1800
# Persistent dedupe state; the systemd service creates /var/lib/econ mode 0700.
# ECON_TELEGRAM_STATE_FILE=/var/lib/econ/telegram-state.json

# Stocks tab headlines (context only; never used by the screen or its ranking).
# Disable the RSS headline lookup entirely:
# ECON_STOCK_NEWS=0
# Keep only headlines published inside this window (1-30):
# ECON_STOCK_NEWS_DAYS=7
# Headlines shown per displayed ticker (1-5):
# ECON_STOCK_NEWS_PER_SYMBOL=3

# Stocks tab history fetch pacing (Sina -> Nasdaq -> Tencent -> Yahoo -> Stooq).
# Vendor WAFs block this IP when 32 symbols burst at once, so keep these polite.
# Minimum seconds between requests to one stock-history host (+jitter):
# ECON_STOCK_PACE=0.3
# Hard cap on HTTP requests per stock-history refresh:
# ECON_STOCK_REQUEST_BUDGET=128

# Economy 101 tab (US vs Malaysia explainer). Annual World Bank series only;
# no extra provider is contacted. History window in years (charts).
# ECON_HISTORY_YEARS=12

# Malaysia's OPR has no stable key-less endpoint, so it is a manual reference
# shown as "manual · as of <date>" on the page. Update both values whenever Bank
# Negara Malaysia changes the rate (bnm.gov.my) and restart the service.
# ECON_MY_OPR=3.00
# ECON_MY_OPR_AS_OF=2023-05-03

# --- Pick tab (best-pick planner) -------------------------------------------
# Same data as the Stocks tab; this only changes how the plan is drawn.
# ECON_PICK=0                  # hide the Pick tab entirely
# ECON_PICK_MIN_STOP_PCT=2.5   # floor for the hard stop, % below the entry
# ECON_PICK_MAX_STOP_PCT=8     # cap: largest loss the plan will ever imply
# ECON_PICK_COST_PCT=0.35      # assumed round-trip cost (commission+spread+FX)
# ECON_PICK_ENTRY_SIGMA=0.6    # buy-zone depth, in one-session sigmas
# ECON_PICK_HOLD_SESSIONS=20   # fallback holding horizon when drift is absent
# ECON_PICK_MAX_VOL=120        # above this 20-session volatility %, no plan is drawn
# ECON_PICK_TZ=Asia/Kuala_Lumpur
